The competing parties simply kill each other.

What a novel idea huh?

Federal laws -- the ADA (Americans with Disabilities Act) -- make specific requirements for 'accessible' parking spaces; these by law must be:
-- located at the shortest accessible route to the accessible entrance to the building or facility; 
-- At least 96 inches (12ft) wide, with an access aisle at least 60 inches (5ft) wide; van-accessible spaces must be at least 13 feet (132) inches wide.

The access aisles (space between each parking-spot) must be at least 60 inches wide, (for those using mobility devices, i.e wheelchairs, walkers, etc.); 

Signage requirements include the international symbol of accessibility and the signs must be mounted at least 60 inches above the ground.

Minimum numbers apply for cars and vans:
one in 25 each (one for cars, another for vans);
one more such spot for where there are 26-50 spaces,
and a third spot if the parking area has 51-75 spaces...
